PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_14meltygui_imgui_4core_484push_item_width, "push_item_width(float item_width)\n\nPush item width in the stack.\n\n**Note:** sizing of child region allows for three modes:\n\n* ``0.0`` - default to ~2/3 of windows width\n* ``>0.0`` - width in pixels\n* ``<0.0`` - align xx pixels to the right of window\n  (so -FLOAT_MIN always align width to the right side)\n\n**Note:** width pushed on stack need to be poped using\n:func:`pop_item_width()` or it will be applied to all subsequent\nchildren components.\n\n.. visual-example::\n    :auto_layout:\n    :width: 200\n    :height: 200\n\n    meltygui_imgui.begin(\"Example: item width\")\n\n    # custom width\n    meltygui_imgui.push_item_width(meltygui_imgui.get_window_width() * 0.33)\n    meltygui_imgui.text('Lorem Ipsum ...')\n    meltygui_imgui.slider_float('float slider', 10.2, 0.0, 20.0, '%.2f', 1.0)\n    meltygui_imgui.pop_item_width()\n\n    # default width\n    meltygui_imgui.text('Lorem Ipsum ...')\n    meltygui_imgui.slider_float('float slider', 10.2, 0.0, 20.0, '%.2f', 1.0)\n\n    meltygui_imgui.end()\n\nArgs:\n    item_width (float): width of the component\n\n.. wraps::\n    void PushItemWidth(float item_width)");
