PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_14meltygui_imgui_4core_566begin_group, "begin_group()\n\nStart item group and lock its horizontal starting position.\n\nCaptures group bounding box into one \"item\". Thanks to this you can use\n:any:`is_item_hovered()` or layout primitives such as :any:`same_line()`\non whole group, etc.\n\n.. visual-example::\n    :auto_layout:\n    :width: 500\n\n    with meltygui_imgui.begin(\"Example: item groups\"):\n\n        with meltygui_imgui.begin_group():\n            meltygui_imgui.text(\"First group (buttons):\")\n            meltygui_imgui.button(\"Button A\")\n            meltygui_imgui.button(\"Button B\")\n\n        meltygui_imgui.same_line(spacing=50)\n\n        with meltygui_imgui.begin_group():\n            meltygui_imgui.text(\"Second group (text and bullet texts):\")\n            meltygui_imgui.bullet_text(\"Bullet A\")\n            meltygui_imgui.bullet_text(\"Bullet B\")\n\nExample::\n\n    meltygui_imgui.begin(\"Example: item groups\")\n\n    meltygui_imgui.begin_group()\n    meltygui_imgui.text(\"First group (buttons):\")\n    meltygui_imgui.button(\"Button A\")\n    meltygui_imgui.button(\"Button B\")\n    meltygui_imgui.end_group()\n\n    meltygui_imgui.same_line(spacing=50)\n\n    meltygui_imgui.begin_group()\n    meltygui_imgui.text(\"Second group (text and bullet texts):\")\n    meltygui_imgui.bullet_text(\"Bullet A\")\n    meltygui_imgui.bullet_text(\"Bullet B\")\n    meltygui_imgui.end_group()\n\n    meltygui_imgui.end()\n\nReturns:\n    _BeginEndGrouop; use with ``with`` to automatically call :func:`end_group` when the block ends.\n\n.. wraps::\n    void BeginGroup()");
